                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Big No\nThe game is challenging I'll give it that, the music loop almost drove me insane thankfully there is a button to stop it, no key rebind, teleporting from inside a wall gives zero coyote time, the water is a hazard that doesn't let you move while it slowly drains away your life, no checkpoints (probably to give it more challenge?), you can shoot but generally is better to simply ignore the enemies with the exception of the drones (because they follow you through all the level) and bosses because you have to kill them, there is no reward into killing any of them\n \nNormally a lot of those things are a nuisance but when you have to teleport, immediately jump, do a second jump ( btw you can't control your jump height at all) avoid a big saw that takes half of your life to get to a wall that you have to teleport in, failing because you missed the perfect spot to teleport in ,and to fall to the ground is a big no, sometimes you have to do this 3 or 5 times in a row which can drive you insane because you feel is the fault of the controller and not yours, a precise platformer should never feel like the controller is getting in the way; as another example there are walls that you have to teleport in with water hazards below and if you are too close or too far away it will refuse to teleport you in and fall to the water slowly killing you or teleport you too far ahead and fall to the other water hazard because there is no coyote time when you teleport and you can't do anything at all, this happens a lot in mid and late parts of a level.\n\nAs a final nitpick the bonus levels indication get lost in the background I got the nine lives achievement before I found the first bonus level by mistake.",
